/target
/regtest-harness/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Local runtime data / wallets (never commit secrets). /data-btc* covers the datadirs the
# Bitcoin dev-stack samples (deploy/zecd.btc-testnet*.toml) document, which sit in the repo
# root because zecd runs on the host there - the entries below catch a datadir's contents but
# not its `.lock`, so without this the directory itself shows up untracked.
/data
/data-btc*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
keys.toml
*.cookie
.cookie
identity.txt
zecd.toml
# Compose reads deploy/.env automatically, and the mainnet stack sources its bitcoind
# rpcauth line from there - so an operator following that file's instructions creates a
# credential-bearing file here. Ignored in the tracked .gitignore (not just a local
# .git/info/exclude) so it is ignored in every clone, not only the one it was written in.
deploy/.env
# ...but the docker-stack template is intentional (a checked-in example, no real secrets).
!/deploy/zecd.toml
__pycache__/
